## 2.4 Real crawler

Implement a genuine crawler that retrieves actual public website pages.

It should discover URLs from:

- Internal links.
- robots.txt.
- XML sitemaps and sitemap indexes.
- Canonical references and related page metadata where appropriate.

The crawler should support configurable:

- Maximum pages.
- Crawl depth.
- Same-domain or permitted subdomain scope.
- URL inclusion/exclusion patterns.
- Request timeouts.
- Bounded concurrency.
- JavaScript rendering when the deployment has a supported rendering engine.

