- URL and final redirected URL.
- HTTP status.
- Response headers.
- Content type.
- Response timing.
- Content length when available.
- Title and meta description.
- H1 and other headings.
- Canonical URL.
- Robots directives.
- Language metadata.
- Internal and external links.
- Image metadata.
- Structured data.
- Actual content text and relevant content metrics.

Deduplicate URLs and prevent crawl traps, infinite paths, repeated parameters, and unbounded resource consumption.

Handle broken pages, redirects, unavailable hosts, rate limits, oversized responses, non-HTML resources, DNS failures, and timeouts gracefully.

Respect applicable crawling rules and reasonable server load.

### SSRF protection

Security is mandatory.

Validate every URL, resolved IP address, redirect hop, and outbound destination.

Block loopback, private, link-local, cloud-metadata, and otherwise prohibited targets. Account for IPv4, IPv6, DNS rebinding, redirects, and discovered URLs.

Prevent the crawler from becoming a proxy into internal networks or server infrastructure.

Never disable SSRF protections just to make a scan work.

